VERDICT: approve
{"verdict":"approve","summary":"I re-read the shrink path and repaint logic; the changed clear span matches the rows that are actually redrawn and avoids erasing still-valid terminal-scrolled history above that span. I do not accept the stale-content objection because the caller already clears the vacated old viewport rows, while rows 0..top are deliberately preserved content that repaint_history_tail must not blank or duplicate.","concede":[],"maintain":["Approve: in set_height's shrink branch, old viewport rows are cleared before viewport.y is moved and repaint_history_tail is called; repaint_history_tail then clears/redraws only top..visible_rows, where top accounts for scrollback_committed lines that must not be redrawn. Clearing 0..top would erase content that remains valid on screen and cannot be restored without duplicating native scrollback."],"findings":[]}
